For any task involving an external provider, read `.agents/skills/provider-integration-research-and-implementation/SKILL.md` plus the corresponding documents in `docs/research/provider-integration/`.

Use current official provider references. Capture API version/status/date, required entitlement, account/market scope, state meanings, time limits and rate limits. Never assume an API listed publicly is enabled for Travelar. Keep provider request/response details behind adapters and Travelar UI provider-neutral. Distinguish offer search, offer validation, booking, ticket issuance, payment receipt, merchant settlement and supplier payout. After timeout on a mutating operation, query/retrieve/reconcile before retry. ClickPesa has no public sandbox, so automated testing must use mocks unless a human explicitly approves a bounded live test. No production enablement without contract, legal/finance, security, operations and human-approval gates.


For operator-side route and recurrence management, seat-map/inventory semantics, data-driven card/forms, staff roles, HIMS payout controls or partner API documentation, also read Documents 76–83 and the `data-driven-platform-operations` skill.


